      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَأْرُوطٌ</span></b>  A hide <i>tanned with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْطًي</span>; (S, K;) i. e.
<i>with the leaves thereof;</i> (S in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رطي</span>;) as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤَرْطًي</span></b> ; (TA;) and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْطِيٌّ</span>. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  A
camel <i>having a complaint from eating</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْطًي</span>:
(L, K: *) and a camel <i>that eats</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْطًي</span>, (AZ, S, K,)
<i>and keeps to it;</i> (K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْطَوِىُّ</span></b>  (AZ, S, K)
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْطَاوِىٌّ</span></b> . (Ibn-'Abbád, Sgh, L, K.)

